        "value_sha256": "2177e260939f6e0dffb1a2a24751626faccd9b59a39d21288199bdc2984ae5f3",
        "weakness_class": "SQL injection (CWE-89) carried in an untrusted log field: a SQL-backed SIEM / log store that string-concatenates the field into a query is exploitable, and a WAF/IDS in front of the web tier should match the injection on the wire. Durable class; the canonical UNION/boolean/time-based/error-based forms below let a defender test detection QUALITY across evasion variants. Carries no real target (no host, no schema-qualified table) — an inert detection-test string only.",
        "expected_defender_signal": "A SQL-backed store must parameterize/bind log fields (never string-concatenate them into a query); a WAF/IDS should match UNION SELECT, OR '1'='1', stacked / time-based (SLEEP/WAITFOR) and error-based (extractvalue) injection on the wire.",
        "ids_alert": {
          "sid": 2009714,
          "rev": 9,
          "message": "ET WEB_SERVER Possible SQL Injection Attempt UNION SELECT"
        }
      }
    },
